- [dermatofibroma Standard]: Dermatofibromas are typically solitary, skin-colored to light brown, firm, round or oval-shaped lesions. They can vary in size from a few millimeters to over 1 centimeter in diameter. The surface of these tumors is usually smooth, with slight blurred or waxy borders and sparse vellus hair. Dermatofibromas often display follicular openings and exhibit minimal signs of inflammation or atrophy. Surrounding skin is generally unaffected. While rare, multiple dermatofibromas can occur, especially in individuals with a genetic predisposition.


